{"schema": "abb.observe.event.v1", "source": "otel-payload", "run_id": "run_020c9dbfac1f4b0e8a1f599fdeca930f", "timestamp": "2026-10-11T15:20:22.365225+00:00", "event": "acp.prompt_started", "data": {"name": "acp.prompt_started", "payload": {"session_id": "f67ad522-4312-406b-8a31-8179c500856e", "input": "Write a formal specification for `add` and `multiply` in a file named `spec.md`. The specification should state that both functions are commutative and associative for all integers, and that `multiply` distributes over `add`."}, "span_event": true, "case_id": "case_7da748ae705d43c7a80c1fa211c2a22d", "input_id": "step-2", "invocation_id": "ee7baf027dfa492bbda0bf03737046ad", "agent_id": "mastracode"}}
{"schema": "abb.observe.event.v1", "source": "otel-payload", "run_id": "run_020c9dbfac1f4b0e8a1f599fdeca930f", "timestamp": "2026-10-11T15:20:22.542083+00:00", "event": "acp.session_update", "data": {"name": "acp.session_update", "payload": {"session_id": "f67ad522-4312-406b-8a31-8179c500856e", "update": {"content": {"text": "Write a formal specification for `add` and `multiply` in a file named `spec.md`. The specification should state that both functions are commutative and associative for all integers, and that `multiply` distributes over `add`.", "type": "text"}, "sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk"}}, "span_event": false, "case_id": "case_7da748ae705d43c7a80c1fa211c2a22d", "input_id": "step-2", "invocation_id": "ee7baf027dfa492bbda0bf03737046ad", "agent_id": "mastracode"}}
{"schema": "abb.observe.event.v1", "source": "otel-payload", "run_id": "run_020c9dbfac1f4b0e8a1f599fdeca930f", "timestamp": "2026-10-11T15:20:32.165128+00:00", "event": "acp.session_update", "data": {"name": "acp.session_update", "payload": {"session_id": "f67ad522-4312-406b-8a31-8179c500856e", "update": {"toolCallId": "call_f04080144ff546bc96301433", "title": "write_file", "kind": "edit", "status": "in_progress", "rawInput": "{\"content\":\"# Specification: `arith.add` and `arith.multiply`\\n\\n## Definitions\\n\\nLet `ℤ` denote the set of all integers. For `a, b ∈ ℤ`:\\n\\n- `add(a, b)` returns the integer sum `a + b`.\\n- `multiply(a, b)` returns the integer product `a * b`.\\n\\nBoth functions are total on `ℤ × ℤ` and always return a value in `ℤ`.\\n\\n## Properties\\n\\n### 1. Commutativity\\n\\nFor all integers `a, b`:\\n\\n```text\\nadd(a, b)      == add(b, a)\\nmultiply(a, b) == multiply(b, a)\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Associativity\\n\\nFor all integers `a, b, c`:\\n\\n```text\\nadd(add(a, b), c)      == add(a, add(b, c))\\nmultiply(multiply(a, b), c) == multiply(a, multiply(b, c))\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Distributivity\\n\\n`multiply` distributes over `add` on both sides:\\n\\nFor all integers `a, b, c`:\\n\\n```text\\nmultiply(a, add(b, c)) == add(multiply(a, b), multiply(a, c))\\nmultiply(add(a, b), c) == add(multiply(a, c), multiply(b, c))\\n```\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- These properties hold for all integers, including negative values and zero.\\n- `add` has identity element `0`: `add(a, 0) == a`.\\n- `multiply` has identity element `1`: `multiply(a, 1) == a`.\\n\",\"path\":\"spec.md\"}", "sessionUpdate": "tool_call"}}, "span_event": false, "case_id": "case_7da748ae705d43c7a80c1fa211c2a22d", "input_id": "step-2", "invocation_id": "ee7baf027dfa492bbda0bf03737046ad", "agent_id": "mastracode"}}
{"schema": "abb.observe.event.v1", "source": "otel-payload", "run_id": "run_020c9dbfac1f4b0e8a1f599fdeca930f", "timestamp": "2026-10-11T15:20:32.172068+00:00", "event": "acp.session_update", "data": {"name": "acp.session_update", "payload": {"session_id": "f67ad522-4312-406b-8a31-8179c500856e", "update": {"toolCallId": "call_f04080144ff546bc96301433", "status": "completed", "rawOutput": "Wrote 1057 bytes to spec.md", "sessionUpdate": "tool_call_update"}}, "span_event": false, "case_id": "case_7da748ae705d43c7a80c1fa211c2a22d", "input_id": "step-2", "invocation_id": "ee7baf027dfa492bbda0bf03737046ad", "agent_id": "mastracode"}}
{"schema": "abb.observe.event.v1", "source": "otel-payload", "run_id": "run_020c9dbfac1f4b0e8a1f599fdeca930f", "timestamp": "2026-10-11T15:20:41.113881+00:00", "event": "acp.session_update", "data": {"name": "acp.session_update", "payload": {"session_id": "f67ad522-4312-406b-8a31-8179c500856e", "update": {"toolCallId": "call_f9078af493be481685d3a923", "title": "execute_command", "kind": "execute", "status": "in_progress", "rawInput": "{\"command\":\"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport random, arith\\nfor _ in range(10000):\\n    a, b, c = (random.randint(-10**6, 10**6) for _ in range(3))\\n    assert arith.add(a, b) == arith.add(b, a)\\n    assert arith.multiply(a, b) == arith.multiply(b, a)\\n    assert arith.add(arith.add(a, b), c) == arith.add(a, arith.add(b, c))\\n    assert arith.multiply(arith.multiply(a, b), c) == arith.multiply(a, arith.multiply(b, c))\\n    assert arith.multiply(a, arith.add(b, c)) == arith.add(arith.multiply(a, b), arith.multiply(a, c))\\n    assert arith.multiply(arith.add(a, b), c) == arith.add(arith.multiply(a, c), arith.multiply(b, c))\\nprint('OK')\\n\\\"\"}", "sessionUpdate": "tool_call"}}, "span_event": false, "case_id": "case_7da748ae705d43c7a80c1fa211c2a22d", "input_id": "step-2", "invocation_id": "ee7baf027dfa492bbda0bf03737046ad", "agent_id": "mastracode"}}
